s\\\",\\n    \\\" src/core/python.js\\\",\\n    \\\" src/data/mockRepositories.ts\\\",\\n    \\\" src/main.tsx\\\",\\n    \\\" src/types/vva.ts\\\",\\n    \\\" src/utils/docxExporter.ts\\\",\\n    \\\" src/utils/orchestrator.ts\\\",\\n    \\\" src/utils/pdfGenerator.ts\\\",\\n    \\\" tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\" vite.config.ts\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"technicalChanges\\\": [\\n    \\\"Added environment example with NVIDIA API key and model configuration\\\",\\n    \\\"Created .gitignore to exclude build artifacts and logs\\\",\\n    \\\"Provided README with local run instructions\\\",\\n    \\\"Implemented ai/ai_engine.py to invoke NVIDIA API for commit analysis\\\",\\n    \\\"Added ai/test_nvidia.py for API connectivity test\\\",\\n    \\\"Created bin/vva.js as CLI entry point\\\",\\n    \\\"Generated bun.lock with full dependency tree\\\",\\n    \\\"Set up index.html and metadata.json for web deployment\\\",\\n    \\\"Included comprehensive project description in public/assets\\\",\\n    \\\"Defined JSON schemas for AI response and project data\\\",\\n    \\\"Built React application entry point (src/App.tsx) and main.tsx\\\",\\n    \\\"Implemented CLI command modules (init, report, status, watch)\\\",\\n    \\\"Implemented core Git utilities for repository detection and data extraction\\\",\\n    \\\"Implemented core collector for gathering commit metadata and diffs\\\",\\n    \\\"Implemented core Python module for invoking AI and document engines\\\",\\n    \\\"Created UI components for terminal, collector, AI engine, document generation, architecture, team, and header\\\",\\n    \\\"Added utility functions for orchestrating data flow and generating structured AI responses\\\",\\n    \\\"Added TypeScript types for VVA data structures\\\",\\n    \\\"Added PDF and Word export utilities\\\",\\n    \\\"Configured TypeScript compiler options and Vite build settings\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"technologies\\\": [\\n    \\\"Node.js\\\",\\n    \\\"TypeScript\\\",\\n    \\\"React\\\",\\n    \\\"Vite\\\",\\n    \\\"Tailwind CSS\\\",\\n    \\\"Express\\\",\\n    \\\"jspdf\\\",\\n    \\\"lucide-react\\\",\\n    \\\"motion\\\",\\n    \\\"dotenv\\\",\\n    \\\"OpenAI SDK\\\",\\n    \\\"NVIDIA API (meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct)\\\",\\n    \\\"Python 3\\\",\\n    \\\"OpenAI Python SDK\\\",\\n    \\\"Bun lockfile\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"architecturalImpact\\\": \\\"The commit establishes a layered architecture: a Node.js orchestrator (CLI & React UI) coordinates Git data collection, AI analysis, and document generation. The AI engine runs in Python, communicating via JSON files. The project is modularized into commands, core utilities, components, and schemas, enabling clear separation of concerns and facilitating future extensions.\\\",\\n  \\\"observationsAndLimitations\\\": [\\n    \\\"The commit only adds files; no functional tests or CI configuration are present.\\\",\\n    \\\"The AI engine script relies on an NVIDIA API key hard‑coded in .env.example, which may not be secure for production.\\\",\\n    \\\"The bun.lock file is extremely large, potentially impacting install times.\\\",\\n    \\\"The project includes both Node.js and Python components but does not provide a unified build or deployment pipeline.\\\",\\n    \\\"No error handling for missing dependencies or environment variables is included in the CLI commands.\\\",\\n    \\\"The React UI references assets that may not be present in the repository root.\\\",\\n    \\\"The commit does not include any documentation for the API endpoints used by the AI engine.\\\",\\n    \\\"The TypeScript configuration uses experimental decorators without corresponding code.\\\",\\n    \\\"The project relies on a specific version of the NVIDIA model (meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct) but does not provide fallback logic.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"confidenceScore\\\": 0.95,\\n  \\\"model\\\": \\\"openai/gpt-oss-20b\\\",\\n  \\\"processingTimeMs\\\": 150596\\n}\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \".vva/output/project-data.json\",\n      \"status\": \"A\",\n      \"additions\": 0,\n      \"deletions\": 0,\n      \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"vvaVersion\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-10-25T10:57:51.722Z\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": \\\"vva-—-workflow\\\",\\n  \\\"repositoryPath\\\": \\\"C:/Users/Abhira/Desktop/Projects/vva-—-workflow\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"main\\\",\\n  \\\"analyzedCommit\\\": \\\"736708e4f9ead74663cb0b8eb47f83046f036f1d\\\",\\n  \\\"parentCommit\\\": \\\"14122d8d3bc39f9bf3cc3cb834a02030f455fff3\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"abhirambinil-08\\\",\\n    \\\"email\\\": \\\"abhiram.binil.08@gmail.com\\\",\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-10-20T18:17:46+05:30\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"commitMessage\\\": \\\"new changes added\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": {\\n    \\\"filesChanged\\\": 1,\\n    \\\"insertions\\\": 242,\\n    \\\"deletions\\\": 13\\n  },\\n  \\\"changedFiles\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"README.md\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"additions\\\": 736708,\\n      \\\"deletions\\\": 13,\\n      \\\"content\\\": \\\"# VVA --- Version & Workflow Automator\\\\n\\\\n**Turn Git changes and project activity into structured, AI-assisted\\\\ndocumentation.**\\\\n\\\\nVVA (Version & Workflow Automator) is a CLI-based developer tool\\\\ndesigned to analyze project changes, use AI to generate meaningful\\\\nsummaries, and automate documentation and report generation.\\\\n\\\\n## Overview\\\\n\\\\nVVA aims to simplify the process of turning software development\\\\nactivity into useful documentation by connecting Git, AI analysis, and\\\\ndocument generation in a single workflow.\\\\n\\\\n## Features\\\\n\\\\n-   **Git Integration:** Collect project information and changed-file\\\\n    details.\\\\n-   **AI-Powered Analysis:** Generate summaries and structured insights\\\\n    using an AI provider.\\\\n-   **Document Generation:** Generate reports in formats such as PDF,\\\\n    DOCX, and PPTX, subject to the current implementation.\\\\n-   **CLI Automation:** Execute workflows through terminal commands.\\\\n-   **Project Monitoring:** Provide a foundation for tracking project\\\\n    changes.\\\\n-   **Python Integration:** Connect Node.js orchestration with\\\\n    Python-based AI and document-processing engines.\\\\n\\\\n> **Status:** VVA is under active development. Features and output\\\\n> formats may vary depending on the current implementation.\\\\n\\\\n## Technology Stack\\\\n\\\\n  Technology                     Purpose\\\\n  ------------------------------ ---------------------------------------\\\\n  Node.js                        CLI and workflow orchestration\\\\n  JavaScript (ES Modules)        Application logic\\\\n  Python                         AI processing and document generation\\\\n  Git                            Version control and change analysis\\\\n  NVIDIA API                     AI inference integration\\\\n  PDF, DOCX and PPTX libraries   Document generation\\\\n\\\\n## Project Structure\\\\n\\\\n``` text\\\\nvva-orchestrator/\\\\n├── bin/\\\\n│   └── vva.js\\\\n├── src/\\\\n│   ├── cli.js\\\\n│   ├── commands/\\\\n│   │   ├── init.js\\\\n│   │   ├── status.js\\\\n│   │   ├── report.js\\\\n│   │   └── watch.js\\\\n│   └── core/\\\\n│       └── python.js\\\\n├── ai/\\\\n│   └── ai_engine.py\\\\n├── document_engine/\\\\n│   └── document_engine.py\\\\n├── .vva/\\\\n│   └── output/\\\\n├── package.json\\\\n└── README.md\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n*This is an illustrative structure; the actual files may differ by\\\\nversion.*\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisites\\\\n\\\\n-   [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/)\\\\n-   [Python](https://www.python.org/)\\\\n-   [Git](https://git-scm.com/)\\\\n-   A valid NVIDIA API key for AI-powered features\\\\n\\\\n## Installation\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Clone the repository\\\\n\\\\n``` bash\\\\ngit clone https://github.com/abhirambinil-08/vva-orchestrator.git\\\\ncd vva-orchestrator\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Install dependencies\\\\n\\\\n``` bash\\\\nnpm install\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nInstall the Python dependencies required by the project. If a\\\\n`requirements.txt` file is available, run:\\\\n\\\\n``` bash\\\\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Configure environment variables\\\\n\\\\nCreate a `.env` file in the project root and add your NVIDIA API key:\\\\n\\\\n``` env\\\\nNVIDIA_API_KEY=your_nvidia_api_key_here\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nReplace the placeholder with your own key.\\\\n\\\\n**Security:** Never commit `.env` files or real API keys. Keep secrets\\\\nout of `.env.example`, generated reports, project snapshots, and Git\\\\nhistory. Use placeholder values in example configuration files.\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\nVVA provides a command-line interface with the following intended\\\\ncommands.\\\\n\\\\n### Initialize a project\\\\n\\\\n``` bash\\\\nvva init\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nInitializes VVA configuration for a project.\\\\n\\\\n### Check project status\\\\n\\\\n``` bash\\\\nvva status\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nDisplays project status and available VVA information.\\\\n\\\\n### Generate a report\\\\n\\\\n``` bash\\\\nvva report\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nRuns the reporting workflow, designed to collect project data, analyze\\\\nchanges with AI, and generate documentation.\\\\n\\\\n### Watch project changes\\\\n\\\\n``` bash\\\\nvva watch\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nStarts the project-monitoring workflow if implemented in the current\\\\nversion.\\\\n\\\\nCommand availability depends on the installed version and project\\\\nconfiguration.\\\\n\\\\n## How It Works\\\\n\\\\nThe intended reporting workflow is:\\\\n\\\\n1.  Collect project metadata and Git changes.\\\\n2.  Prepare the relevant change data for analysis.\\\\n3.  Send the data to the configured AI engine.\\\\n4.  Process the AI response into structured documentation.\\\\n5.  Generate reports through the document engine.\\\\n6.  Save the generated artifacts to the configured output directory.\\\\n\\\\n## Output Formats\\\\n\\\\nVVA is designed to support structured project documentation and reports,\\\\npotentially including:\\\\n\\\\n-   **PDF** --- Shareable project reports.\\\\n-   **DOCX** --- Editable documentation.\\\\n-   **PPTX** --- Presentation-style reports.\\\\n-   **JSON** --- Intermediate project and AI analysis data.\\\\n\\\\nActual formats depend on the current implementation.\\\\n\\\\n## Troubleshooting\\\\n\\\\n### AI analysis fails\\\\n\\\\n-   Verify that the NVIDIA API key is valid.\\\\n-   Confirm that environment variables are loaded correctly.\\\\n-   Check network connectivity and provider availability.\\\\n-   Review AI response errors and token limits.\\\\n\\\\n### Python engine fails\\\\n\\\\n-   Verify that Python is installed.\\\\n-   Install the required dependencies.\\\\n-   Check that the CLI resolves the correct project root and Python\\\\n    script paths.\\\\n\\\\n### `vva` command is not recognized\\\\n\\\\n-   Confirm that Node.js dependencies are installed.\\\\n-   Check the `bin` entry in `package.json`.\\\\n-   Link the package locally if needed for development.\\\\n\\\\n### Git push is rejected\\\\n\\\\nIf Git reports a non-fast-forward error, fetch the remote and inspect\\\\nthe branch history before integrating changes. Avoid force-pushing until\\\\nyou've verified that remote commits will not be lost and sensitive\\\\ninformation will not be exposed.\\\\n\\\\n## Roadmap\\\\n\\\\nPotential future improvements include:\\\\n\\\\n-   More reliable Git change analysis.\\\\n-   Improved AI response validation and error handling.\\\\n-   Additional document templates.\\\\n-   Automated documentation through watch mode.\\\\n-   Student practical-file generation.\\\\n-   Configurable project-specific documentation.\\\\n-   An optional centralized service for team and enterprise workflows.\\\\n\\\\nRoadmap items are planned ideas, not claims of completed functionality.\\\\n\\\\n## Contributing\\\\n\\\\nContributions, bug reports, and suggestions are welcome.\\\\n\\\\n1.  Fork the repository.\\\\n2.  Create a feature branch.\\\\n3.  Implement and test your changes.\\\\n4.  Submit a pull request describing your changes.\\\\n\\\\nDo not include API keys, credentials, private project data, or sensitive\\\\ngenerated reports in commits.\\\\n\\\\n## License\\\\n\\\\nNo license has been specified yet. Add a license file if you intend to\\\\ndefine permissions for reuse and redistribution.\\\\n\\\\n## Author\\\\n\\\\n**Abhiram Binil**\\\\n\\\\n-   GitHub: [@abhirambinil-08](https://github.com/abhirambinil-08)\\\\n\\\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n\\\\n*VVA --- Automating the journey from code changes to clear\\\\ndocumentation.*\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"diff\\\": \\\"diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\\\nindex 46a485d..cb4b9ac 100644\\\\n--- a/README.md\\\\n+++ b/README.md\\\\n@@ -1,20 +1,249 @@\\\\n-<div align=\\\\\\\"center\\\\\\\">\\\\n-<img width=\\\\\\\"1200\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"475\\\\\\\" alt=\\\\\\\"GHBanner\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://ai.google.dev/static/site-assets/images/share-ais-513315318.png\\\\\\\" />\\\\n-</div>\\\\n+# VVA --- Version & Workflow Automator\\\\n \\\\n-# Run and deploy your AI Studio app\\\\n+**Turn Git changes and project activity into structured, AI-assisted\\\\n+documentation.**\\\\n \\\\n-This contains everything you need to run your app locally.\\\\n+VVA (Version & Workflow Automator) is a CLI-based developer tool\\\\n+designed to analyze project changes, use AI to generate meaningful\\\\n+summaries, and automate documentation and report generation.\\\\n \\\\n-View your app in AI Studio: https://ai.studio/apps/1b38b727-e650-4847-b6aa-afb66d9b3f65\\\\n+## Overview\\\\n \\\\n-## Run Locally\\\\n+VVA aims to simplify the process of turning software development\\\\n+activity into useful documentation by connecting Git, AI analysis, and\\\\n+document generation in a single workflow.\\\\n \\\\n-**Prerequisites:**  Node.js\\\\n+## Features\\\\n \\\\n+-   **Git Integration:** Collect project information and changed-file\\\\n+    details.\\\\n+-   **AI-Powered Analysis:** Generate summaries and structured insights\\\\n+    using an AI provider.\\\\n+-   **Document Generation:** Generate reports in formats such as PDF,\\\\n+    DOCX, and PPTX, subject to the current implementation.\\\\n+-   **CLI Automation:** Execute workflows through terminal commands.\\\\n+-   **Project Monitoring:** Provide a foundation for tracking project\\\\n+    changes.\\\\n+-   **Python Integration:** Connect Node.js orchestration with\\\\n+    Python-based AI and document-processing engines.\\\\n \\\\n-1. Install dependencies:\\\\n-   `npm install`\\\\n-2. Set the `GEMINI_API_KEY` in [.env.local](.env.local) to your Gemini API key\\\\n-3. Run the app:\\\\n-   `npm run dev`\\\\n+> **Status:** VVA is under active development. Features and output\\\\n+> formats may vary depending on the current implementation.\\\\n+\\\\n+## Technology Stack\\\\n+\\\\n+  Technology                     Purpose\\\\n+  ------------------------------ ---------------------------------------\\\\n+  Node.js                        CLI and workflow orchestration\\\\n+  JavaScript (ES Modules)        Application logic\\\\n+  Python                         AI processing and document generation\\\\n+  Git                            Version control and change analysis\\\\n+  NVIDIA API                     AI inference integration\\\\n+  PDF, DOCX and PPTX libraries   Document generation\\\\n+\\\\n+## Project Structure\\\\n+\\\\n+``` text\\\\n+vva-orchestrator/\\\\n+├── bin/\\\\n+│   └── vva.js\\\\n+├── src/\\\\n+│   ├── cli.js\\\\n+│   ├── commands/\\\\n+│   │   ├── init.js\\\\n+│   │   ├── status.js\\\\n+│   │   ├── report.js\\\\n+│   │   └── watch.js\\\\n+│   └── core/\\\\n+│       └── python.js\\\\n+├── ai/\\\\n+│   └── ai_engine.py\\\\n+├── document_engine/\\\\n+│   └── document_engine.py\\\\n+├── .vva/\\\\n+│   └── output/\\\\n+├── package.json\\\\n+└── README.md\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+*This is an illustrative structure; the actual files may differ by\\\\n+version.*\\\\n+\\\\n+## Prerequisites\\\\n+\\\\n+-   [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/)\\\\n+-   [Python](https://www.python.org/)\\\\n+-   [Git](https://git-scm.com/)\\\\n+-   A valid NVIDIA API key for AI-powered features\\\\n+\\\\n+## Installation\\\\n+\\\\n+### 1. Clone the repository\\\\n+\\\\n+``` bash\\\\n+git clone https://github.com/abhirambinil-08/vva-orchestrator.git\\\\n+cd vva-orchestrator\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+### 2. Install dependencies\\\\n+\\\\n+``` bash\\\\n+npm install\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+Install the Python dependencies required by the project. If a\\\\n+`requirements.txt` file is available, run:\\\\n+\\\\n+``` bash\\\\n+python -m pip install -r requirements.txt\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+### 3. Configure environment variables\\\\n+\\\\n+Create a `.env` file in the project root and add your NVIDIA API key:\\\\n+\\\\n+``` env\\\\n+NVIDIA_API_KEY=your_nvidia_api_key_here\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+Replace the placeholder with your own key.\\\\n+\\\\n+**Security:** Never commit `.env` files or real API keys. Keep secrets\\\\n+out of `.env.example`, generated reports, project snapshots, and Git\\\\n+history. Use placeholder values in example configuration files.\\\\n+\\\\n+## Usage\\\\n+\\\\n+VVA provides a command-line interface with the following intended\\\\n+commands.\\\\n+\\\\n+### Initialize a project\\\\n+\\\\n+``` bash\\\\n+vva init\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+Initializes VVA configuration for a project.\\\\n+\\\\n+### Check project status\\\\n+\\\\n+``` bash\\\\n+vva status\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+Displays project status and available VVA information.\\\\n+\\\\n+### Generate a report\\\\n+\\\\n+``` bash\\\\n+vva report\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+Runs the reporting workflow, designed to collect project data, analyze\\\\n+changes with AI, and generate documentation.\\\\n+\\\\n+### Watch project changes\\\\n+\\\\n+``` bash\\\\n+vva watch\\\\n+```\\\\n+\\\\n+Starts the project-monitoring workflow if implemented in the current\\\\n+version.\\\\n+\\\\n+Command availability depends on the installed version and project\\\\n+configuration.\\\\n+\\\\n+## How It Works\\\\n+\\\\n+The intended reporting workflow is:\\\\n+\\\\n+1.  Collect project metadata and Git changes.\\\\n+2.  Prepare the relevant change data for analysis.\\\\n+3.  Send the data to the configured AI engine.\\\\n+4.  Process the AI response into structured documentation.\\\\n+5.  Generate reports through the document engine.\\\\n+6.  Save the generated artifacts to the configured output directory.\\\\n+\\\\n+## Output Formats\\\\n+\\\\n+VVA is designed to support structured project documentation and reports,\\\\n+potentially including:\\\\n+\\\\n+-   **PDF** --- Shareable project reports.\\\\n+-   **DOCX** --- Editable documentation.\\\\n+-   **PPTX** --- Presentation-style reports.\\\\n+-   **JSON** --- Intermediate project and AI analysis data.\\\\n+\\\\n+Actual formats depend on the current implementation.\\\\n+\\\\n+## Troubleshooting\\\\n+\\\\n+### AI analysis fails\\\\n+\\\\n+-   Verify that the NVIDIA API key is valid.\\\\n+-   Confirm that environment variables are loaded correctly.\\\\n+-   Check network connectivity and provider availability.\\\\n+-   Review AI response errors and token limits.\\\\n+\\\\n+### Python engine fails\\\\n+\\\\n+-   Verify that Python is installed.\\\\n+-   Install the required dependencies.\\\\n+-   Check that the CLI resolves the correct project root and Python\\\\n+    script paths.\\\\n+\\\\n+### `vva` command is not recognized\\\\n+\\\\n+-   Confirm that Node.js dependencies are installed.\\\\n+-   Check the `bin` entry in `package.json`.\\\\n+-   Link the package locally if needed for development.\\\\n+\\\\n+### Git push is rejected\\\\n+\\\\n+If Git reports a non-fast-forward error, fetch the remote and inspect\\\\n+the branch history before integrating changes. Avoid force-pushing until\\\\n+you've verified that remote commits will not be lost and sensitive\\\\n+information will not be exposed.\\\\n+\\\\n+## Roadmap\\\\n+\\\\n+Potential future improvements include:\\\\n+\\\\n+-   More reliable Git change analysis.\\\\n+-   Improved AI response validation and error handling.\\\\n+-   Additional document templates.\\\\n+-   Automated documentation through watch mode.\\\\n+-   Student practical-file generation.\\\\n+-   Configurable project-specific documentation.\\\\n+-   An optional centralized service for team and enterprise workflows.\\\\n+\\\\n+Roadmap items are planned ideas, not claims of completed functionality.\\\\n+\\\\n+## Contributing\\\\n+\\\\n+Contributions, bug reports, and suggestions are welcome.\\\\n+\\\\n+1.  Fork the repository.\\\\n+2.  Create a feature branch.\\\\n+3.  Implement and test your changes.\\\\n+4.  Submit a pull request describing your changes.\\\\n+\\\\n+Do not include API keys, credentials, private project data, or sensitive\\\\n+generated reports in commits.\\\\n+\\\\n+## License\\\\n+\\\\n+No license has been specified yet. Add a license file if you intend to\\\\n+define permissions for reuse and redistribution.\\\\n+\\\\n+## Author\\\\n+\\\\n+**Abhiram Binil**\\\\n+\\\\n+-   GitHub: [@abhirambinil-08](https://github.com/abhirambinil-08)\\\\n+\\\\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n+\\\\n+*VVA --- Automating the journey from code changes to clear\\\\n+documentation.*\\\"\\n}\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \".vva/output/vva-_-version-_-workflow-automator_52665ed_presentation.pptx\",\n      \"status\": \"A\",\n      \"additions\": 0,\n      \"deletions\": 0,\n      \"content\": \"PK\\u0003\\u0004\\u0014\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000\\b\\u00009vT]�!�F\\u000b\\u0002\\u0000\\u0000q\\u0017\\u0000\\u0000\\u0013\\u0000\\u0000\\u0000[Content_Types].xml͘�n�0\\u0010��}\\nA\\u0017\\u001d\\n���f��\\u001c���%@�\\u0007`��͔\\u001bHڍ߾#y��&��� /6(���ih�cpt� x�\\u0000c��uqT\\u000e�\\fd�Z&�u�����Ȭ���\\\\I��%��b�at��`3L���g��sBl3\\u0003Am�4Hܙ(#�å�\\u0012M�?t\\n�\\u001a\\u000e�I��\\u0003�\