ica,\\\"Apple Color Emoji\\\",Arial,sans-serif,\\\"Segoe UI Emoji\\\",\\\"Segoe UI Symbol\\\";}DeveloperVVA CLI - Node.jsGit CollectorCommit Metadata, FileVersions and DiffsStructured Project Data JSONPython AI EngineNVIDIA APIStructured AI Response JSONPython Document EnginePDF / DOCX / PPTOutput Directory\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nThe data exchange between modules should have clearly defined formats. This will allow each teammate to develop and test their module independently before the components are integrated.\\n8. VVA command-line interface\\nVVA is designed as a CLI tool so that developers can use it from their existing development environment without needing a separate graphical application.\\nThe main commands have distinct responsibilities.\\nvva init\\nInitializes VVA for a project, checks the Git repository, and creates VVA configuration, logging and output directories.\\nvva status\\nDisplays repository information, current branch, Git status, latest commit and whether VVA has been initialized.\\nvva report\\nCollects Git data, invokes the AI and document modules, and ultimately produces a technical report through the integrated workflow.\\nvva watch\\nIntended to monitor development activity and trigger collection and documentation when relevant changes or commits are detected.\\n\\nThe key difference is that vva report is intended to execute the full pipeline, while vva status provides information and vva init prepares the environment.\\nvva watch is a later automation feature. Monitoring Git activity, triggering the AI and generating documents automatically should be treated as separate implementation milestones, not assumed to be complete just because the command exists.\\n9. Example of a complete VVA workflow\\nSuppose a developer is working on an online ticket-management application.\\nThey add ticket filtering and commit the change:\\ngit add .\\ngit commit -m \\\"Add ticket filtering\\\"\\n\\n\\nThe intended VVA workflow is:\\nStep 1 — Collect the development activity\\nVVA identifies the repository and commit, then retrieves the changed files, commit metadata, relevant committed file versions and diff.\\nStep 2 — Build the project-data JSON\\nVVA stores the collected information in a structured format, such as:\\n{\\n  \\\"repository\\\": \\\"MiniDesk\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"main\\\",\\n  \\\"analyzedCommit\\\": \\\"abc123\\\",\\n  \\\"changedFiles\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"src/tickets/ticket.controller.js\\\",\\n      \\\"content\\\": \\\"[Committed file content]\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"diff\\\": \\\"[Commit-specific patch]\\\"\\n}\\n\\n\\nThis is an illustrative example; the real paths and values depend on the repository.\\nStep 3 — Analyze the work\\nThe Python AI engine receives the project data and identifies the implementation details supported by the code changes.\\nStep 4 — Prepare the document data\\nThe AI returns a structured explanation that can be reused by different document templates.\\nStep 5 — Generate the output\\nThe document engine uses that information to create a report, synopsis or presentation, and VVA saves the result to its output directory.\\nStep 6 — Report the result\\nThe CLI tells the developer which files were generated and where they were saved.\\nThis end-to-end workflow is the main demonstration VVA should ultimately support.\\n10. Team responsibilities\\nThe project is divided among three team members, with each responsible for a separate layer of the system.\\nPerson 1 — Abhiram Binil\\nNode.js · Git · Orchestration\\nAbhiram develops the CLI and the central workflow controller. His work includes repository detection, Git operations, commit-specific data collection, file-system management, JSON handling, Python process communication, integration, and error handling.\\n\\n\\nPerson 2 — Vishnu G Pillai\\nPython · AI · NVIDIA API\\nVishnu develops the AI engine that receives project data, analyzes commit messages and code changes, and returns structured technical explanations for the document-generation module.\\n\\n\\nPerson 3 — Vinay Bisht\\nPython · Document Generation\\nVinay develops the PDF, DOCX and PowerPoint generation modules, including templates, formatting and the conversion of structured AI output into final documents.\\n\\n\\nAlthough the work is divided, all three members need to understand the complete workflow and be able to explain their contributions during the project presentation and viva.\\n11. Technology stack\\nThe planned technologies are organized by responsibility.\\nLayer\\tTechnology\\tPurpose\\nCLI and orchestration\\tNode.js, JavaScript ES modules\\tCommands, process coordination and workflow control\\nVersion control\\tGit\\tCommit history, diffs, file versions and repository metadata\\nData exchange\\tJSON\\tTransfer project data and AI results between modules\\nAI engine\\tPython, NVIDIA API\\tAnalyze changes and generate structured explanations\\nDocument generation\\tPython\\tCreate and format documents\\nPDF output\\tReportLab\\tGenerate PDF reports\\nDOCX output\\tpython-docx\\tCreate editable Word documents\\nPPT output\\tpython-pptx\\tGenerate PowerPoint presentations\\nThe libraries listed are planned implementation choices. They should be considered part of the completed stack only when they have actually been integrated and tested.\\n12. Configuration, files and data management\\nVVA needs to manage both its own configuration and the data it generates.\\nAn intended project layout could look like this:\\nvva/\\n├── package.json\\n├── README.md\\n├── .gitignore\\n├── src/\\n│   ├── commands/\\n│   │   ├── init.js\\n│   │   ├── status.js\\n│   │   ├── report.js\\n│   │   └── watch.js\\n│   └── core/\\n│       ├── git.js\\n│       ├── collector.js\\n│       └── python.js\\n├── ai/\\n│   └── ai_engine.py\\n├── document-engine/\\n│   └── document_generator.py\\n├── docs/\\n├── examples/\\n└── .vva/\\n    ├── config.json\\n    ├── logs/\\n    └── output/\\n\\n\\nThis is a proposed structure and may differ from the actual repository as development progresses.\\nThe .vva directory stores VVA-specific configuration, logs and generated output. The repository's Git metadata and the developer's source code remain managed by Git and the existing project.\\nConfiguration should eventually support settings such as the default document format, output directory and Python environment. Sensitive API keys should be kept out of source control.\\n13. Important engineering considerations\\nFor VVA to generate useful documentation, collecting data successfully is not enough. The workflow must also be reliable.\\nAccuracy: Analyze the exact commit being documented and avoid mixing changes from unrelated commits.\\nError handling: Handle repositories without commits, missing parent commits, deleted files, missing Python installations and failed AI requests.\\nData size: Large diffs or entire source files may exceed AI model limits. VVA should select relevant context, limit payload size where necessary and report when information has been omitted.\\nSecurity and privacy: Source code can contain credentials or confidential information. VVA should avoid sending secrets to an external AI service, protect API keys, and provide appropriate control over which files and diffs are processed.\\nOutput validation: The AI's response should be checked against an expected schema before document generation begins.\\nTraceability: Each generated report should identify the repository and commit it describes, so the developer can trace the documentation back to the underlying development work.\\nThese considerations are part of making VVA a dependable engineering tool rather than a demonstration that works only for one sample commit.\\n14. Current development status\\nBased on the work discussed so far, VVA has an initial implementation of its Node.js foundation.\\nImplemented or tested in earlier steps\\n- CLI initialization and status commands.\\n- Git repository detection and basic Git operations.\\n- Collection of commit metadata and changed files.\\n- Collection of Git diffs.\\n- Saving project data to .vva/output/project-data.json.\\n- Initial Node.js-to-Python process communication.\\n- Retrieving the previous file version for deleted files.\\n\\n\\n\\nRemaining work to verify or complete\\n- Accurate collection of changes for a selected commit, including edge cases.\\n- Robust validation and error handling.\\n- Integration with Vishnu's NVIDIA-powered AI engine.\\n- Integration with Vinay's document-generation module.\\n- A complete vva report workflow that generates a real document.\\n- Automatic monitoring through vva watch.\\n- End-to-end testing, documentation and demonstration preparation.\\n\\n\\n\\nThe exact status of the latest commit-specific collector changes and the other teammates' modules still needs to be verified. A successful Git collection test does not by itself mean the full AI-to-document pipeline is finished.\\n15. Future scope\\nOnce the core workflow is reliable, VVA could be extended with additional capabilities.\\n- Pull request documentation: Generate summaries from pull-request changes and merge history.\\n- Release notes: Summarize changes across a range of commits or a release.\\n- Scheduled progress reports: Generate periodic development summaries.\\n- Custom document templates: Allow teams to select report formats and section layouts.\\n- Multiple projects: Manage documentation workflows for multiple repositories.\\n- Configurable automation: Let users decide when VVA should run and which outputs it should generate.\\n- Improved change analysis: Group related commits and identify larger features across several files.\\n- Additional integrations: Connect to issue trackers or project-management systems if the project later requires them.\\nThese are potential extensions, not features that need to be completed for the first working version.\\n16. Expected outcome\\nThe expected outcome is a functional command-line application that connects Git, AI-assisted analysis and automated document generation.\\nA successful implementation should demonstrate that:\\n1. A developer can initialize VVA in a Git project.\\n2. VVA can collect accurate information about a real commit and its code changes.\\n3. The collected data can be passed to an AI engine.\\n4. The AI engine can return structured, usable analysis.\\n5. The document engine can transform that analysis into a formatted document.\\n6. VVA can coordinate the process and report the location of the generated output.\\nThe project can be useful in academic software projects, development teams, progress reporting, technical documentation and project presentation preparation.\\n17. The core value of VVA\\nVVA's main contribution is automating the journey from software development activity to technical documentation.\\nWithout VVA, developers may need to review Git history, interpret changes, write explanations and format documents as separate tasks. VVA aims to coordinate those activities through a single workflow.\\nIts defining idea is:\\nGit records the work → AI explains the work → the document engine presents the work → VVA coordinates everything.\\nThat is the complete vision of VVA — Version & Workflow Automato\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"schemas/ai-response.schema.json\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"VVAAIResponse\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n  \\\"required\\\": [\\n    \\\"title\\\",\\n    \\\"summary\\\",\\n    \\\"purposeAndRationale\\\",\\n    \\\"changedComponents\\\",\\n    \\\"technicalChanges\\\",\\n    \\\"technologies\\\",\\n    \\\"architecturalImpact\\\",\\n    \\\"observationsAndLimitations\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"properties\\\": {\\n    \\\"title\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"summary\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"purposeAndRationale\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"changedComponents\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" }\\n    },\\n    \\\"technicalChanges\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" }\\n    },\\n    \\\"technologies\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" }\\n    },\\n    \\\"architecturalImpact\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"observationsAndLimitations\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" }\\n    },\\n    \\\"confidenceScore\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\" },\\n    \\\"model\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"processingTimeMs\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\" }\\n  }\\n}\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"schemas/project-data.schema.json\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"VVAProjectData\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n  \\\"required\\\": [\\n    \\\"vvaVersion\\\",\\n    \\\"timestamp\\\",\\n    \\\"repository\\\",\\n    \\\"repositoryPath\\\",\\n    \\\"branch\\\",\\n    \\\"analyzedCommit\\\",\\n    \\\"author\\\",\\n    \\\"commitMessage\\\",\\n    \\\"summary\\\",\\n    \\\"changedFiles\\\",\\n    \\\"diff\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"properties\\\": {\\n    \\\"vvaVersion\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"timestamp\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"repository\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"repositoryPath\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"branch\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"analyzedCommit\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"parentCommit\\\": { \\\"type\\\": [\\\"string\\\", \\\"null\\\"] },\\n    \\\"author\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"name\\\", \\\"email\\\", \\\"date\\\"],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"name\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"email\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"date\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"commitMessage\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"summary\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\\"filesChanged\\\", \\\"insertions\\\", \\\"deletions\\\"],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"filesChanged\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"insertions\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n        \\\"deletions\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"changedFiles\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n        \\\"required\\\": [\\\"file\\\", \\\"status\\\", \\\"additions\\\", \\\"deletions\\\", \\\"content\\\"],\\n        \\\"properties\\\": {\\n          \\\"file\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n          \\\"status\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\", \\\"enum\\\": [\\\"A\\\", \\\"M\\\", \\\"D\\\", \\\"R\\\"] },\\n          \\\"additions\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n          \\\"deletions\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\" },\\n          \\\"content\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"diff\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" },\\n    \\\"warnings\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": { \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\" }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/App.tsx\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import React, { useState } from 'react';\\nimport { Header } from './components/Header';\\nimport { TerminalView } from './components/TerminalView';\\nimport { GitCollectorView } from './components/GitCollectorView';\\nimport { AIEngineView } from './components/AIEngineView';\\nimport { DocumentEngineView } from './components/DocumentEngineView';\\nimport { ArchitectureView } from './components/ArchitectureView';\\nimport { TeamVivaView } from './components/TeamVivaView';\\nimport { SAMPLE_REPOSITORIES, INITIAL_VVA_CONFIG } from './data/mockRepositories';\\nimport { Repository, GitCommit, VVAConfig, ProjectDataJSON, AIStructuredResponse } from './types/vva';\\nimport { buildProjectDataJSON, generateStructuredAIResponse } from './utils/orchestrator';\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  const [repositories, setRepositories] = useState<Repository[]>(SAMPLE_REPOSITORIES);\\n  const [currentRepo, setCurrentRepo] = useState<Repository>(SAMPLE_REPOSITORIES[0]);\\n  const [selectedCommit, setSelectedCommit] = useState<GitCommit>(SAMPLE_REPOSITORIES[0].commits[0]);\\n  const [vvaConfig, setVvaConfig] = useState<VVAConfig>(INITIAL_VVA_CONFIG);\\n  const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState<string>('terminal');\\n  const [isInitialized, setIsInitialized] = useState<boolean>(true);\\n  const [isWatchMode, setIsWatchMode] = useState<boolean>(false);\\n  const [isRunningReport, setIsRunningReport] = useState<boolean>(false);\\n\\n  // Computed / cached data\\n  const initialProjectData = buildProjectDataJSON(currentRepo, selectedCommit, vvaConfig);\\n  const initialAIResponse = generateStructuredAIResponse(initialProjectData, vvaConfig.aiProvider);\\n\\n  const [lastProjectData, setLastProjectData] = useState<ProjectDataJSON>(initialProjectData);\\n  const [lastAIResponse, setLastAIResponse] = useState<AIStructuredResponse>(initialAIResponse);\\n\\n  const handleAddNewCommit = (newCommit: GitCommit) => {\\n    const updatedRepos = repositories.map(repo => {\\n      if (repo.id === currentRepo.id) {\\n        return {\\n          ...repo,\\n          commits: [newCommit, ...repo.commits]\\n        };\\n      }\\n      return repo;\\n    });\\n\\n    setRepositories(updatedRepos);\\n    const updatedCurrent = updatedRepos.find(r => r.id === currentRepo.id) || currentRepo;\\n    setCurrentRepo(updatedCurrent);\\n    setSelectedCommit(newCommit);\\n\\n    // Recompute\\n    const pData = buildProjectDataJSON(updatedCurrent, newCommit, vvaConfig);\\n    const aiResp = generateStructuredAIResponse(pData, vvaConfig.aiProvider);\\n    setLastProjectData(pData);\\n    setLastAIResponse(aiResp);\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleSelectCommit = (commit: GitCommit) => {\\n    setSelectedCommit(commit);\\n    const pData = buildProjectDataJSON(currentRepo, commit, vvaConfig);\\n    const aiResp = generateStructuredAIResponse(pData, vvaConfig.aiProvider);\\n    setLastProjectData(pData);\\n    setLastAIResponse(aiResp);\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleExecuteReport = async (format?: string) => {\\n    setIsRunningReport(true);\\n    return new Promise<void>((resolve) => {\\n      setTimeout(() => {\\n        const pData = buildProjectDataJSON(currentRepo, selectedCommit, vvaConfig);\\n        const aiResp = generateStructuredAIResponse(pData, vvaConfig.aiProvider);\\n        setLastProjectData(pData);\\n        setLastAIResponse(aiResp);\\n        setIsRunningReport(false);\\n        resolve();\\n      }, 700);\\n    });\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleHeaderRunReport = async () => {\\n    await handleExecuteReport();\\n    setActiveTab('documents');\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"min-h-screen bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 flex flex-col font-sans\\\">\\n      {/* Top Bar Contract Header */}\\n      <Header\\n        activeTab={activeTab}\\n        setActiveTab={setActiveTab}\\n        onRunReport={handleHeaderRunReport}\\n        isRunningReport={isRunningReport}\\n        repoName={currentRepo.name}\\n        currentBranch={currentRepo.currentBranch}\\n      />\\n\\n      {/* Main Viewport Content */}\\n      <main className=\\\"flex-1 flex flex-col\\\">\\n        {activeTab === 'terminal' && (\\n          <TerminalView\\n            currentRepo={currentRepo}\\n            selectedCommit={selectedCommit}\\n            vvaConfig={vvaConfig}\\n            isInitialized={isInitialized}\\n            setIsInitialized={setIsInitialized}\\n            onExecuteReport={handleExecuteReport}\\n            isWatchMode={isWatchMode}\\n            setIsWatchMode={setIsWatchMode}\\n            lastProjectData={lastProjectData}\\n            lastAIResponse={lastAIResponse}\\n            onSelectTab={setActiveTab}\\n          />\\n        )}\\n\\n        {activeTab === 'collector' && (\\n          <GitCollectorView\\n            repositories={repositories}\\n            currentRepo={currentRepo}\\n            onSelectRepo={(r) => {\\n              setCurrentRepo(r);\\n              setSelectedCommit(r.commits[0]);\\n              const pData = buildProjectDataJSON(r, r.commits[0], vvaConfig);\\n              const aiResp = generateStructuredAIResponse(pData, vvaConfig.aiProvider);\\n              setLastProjectData(pData);\\n              setLastAIResponse(aiResp);\\n            }}\\n            selectedCommit={selectedCommit}\\n            onSelectCommit={handleSelectCommit}\\n            vvaConfig={vvaConfig}\\n            onAddNewCommit={handleAddNewCommit}\\n          />\\n        )}\\n\\n        {activeTab === 'ai-engine' && (\\n          <AIEngineView\\n            currentRepo={currentRepo}\\n            selectedCommit={selectedCommit}\\n            vvaConfig={vvaConfig}\\n            lastAIResponse={lastAIResponse}\\n            onUpdateAIResponse={setLastAIResponse}\\n          />\\n        )}\\n\\n        {activeTab === 'documents' && (\\n          <DocumentEngineView\\n            currentRepo={currentRepo}\\n            selectedCommit={selectedCommit}\\n            projectData={lastProjectData}\\n            aiAnalysis={lastAIResponse}\\n            vvaConfig={vvaConfig}\\n          />\\n        )}\\n\\n        {activeTab === 'architecture' && <ArchitectureView />}\\n\\n        {activeTab === 'team' && <TeamVivaView />}\\n      </main>\\n\\n      {/* Quiet, Clean Editorial Footer (Anti-Slop Restraint) */}\\n      <footer className=\\\"border-t border-slate-900 bg-slate-950 px-6 py-4 text-xs text-slate-500 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4\\\">\\n        <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n          <span className=\\\"font-semibold text-slate-400\\\">VVA — Version &amp; Workflow Automator</span>\\n          <span>·</span>\\n          <span>Orchestrating Git Commit History into Technical Documents</span>\\n        </div>\\n        <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-4 text-slate-400 font-mono text-[11px]\\\">\\n          <span>Lead Orchestrator: Abhiram Binil</span>\\n          <span>·</span>\\n          <span>AI Engine: Vishnu G Pillai</span>\\n          <span>·</span>\\n          <span>Doc Engine: Vinay Bisht</span>\\n        </div>\\n      </footer>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/cli.js\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env node\\n\\nimport { initCommand } from './commands/init.js';\\nimport { statusCommand } from './commands/status.js';\\nimport { reportCommand } from './commands/report.js';\\nimport { watchCommand } from './commands/watch.js';\\n\\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\\nconst command = args[0]?.toLowerCase();\\n\\nfunction printHelp() {\\n  console.log(`\\nVVA — Version & Workflow Automator [Node.js Orchestrator CLI v1.0.0]\\nUsage: vva <command> [options]\\n\\nCommands:\\n  init                     Initialize .vva/ configuration and output directories\\n  status                   Inspect repository branch, active commit, and VVA status\\n  report [options]         Execute full pipeline: Git -> AI -> PDF/DOCX/PPTX\\n  watch                    Daemon mode: monitor Git commits and auto-generate reports\\n  help                     Show this help guide\\n\\nReport Options:\\n  --commit <hash>          Specify target commit hash (default: HEAD)\\n  --format <pdf|docx|pptx|all> (default: all)\\n  --dry-run                Collect Git data only without invoking Python AI\\n`);\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  if (!command || command === 'help' || command === '--help' || command === '-h') {\\n    printHelp();\\n    process.exit(0);\\n  }\\n\\n  try {\\n    if (command === 'init') {\\n      const res = await initCommand();\\n      console.log(`\\\\x1b[32m✓ VVA successfully initialized in ${res.root}\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n      console.log(`  Created directory: .vva/`);\\n      console.log(`  Created config:    .vva/config.json`);\\n      console.log(`  Created output:    .vva/output/`);\\n      console.log(`\\\\nRun 'vva status' to check environment or 'vva report' to generate documents.`);\\n      process.exit(0);\\n    }\\n\\n    if (command === 'status') {\\n      const res = await statusCommand();\\n      if (!res.isGitRepo) {\\n        console.error(`\\\\x1b[31mError: ${res.message}\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n        process.exit(1);\\n      }\\n\\n      console.log('\\\\x1b[36m=== VVA Repository Status ===\\\\x1b[0m');\\n      console.log(`Repository:      ${res.repositoryName} (${res.repositoryPath})`);\\n      console.log(`Current Branch:  ${res.branch}`);\\n      if (res.latestCommit) {\\n        console.log(`HEAD Commit:     ${res.latestCommit.shortHash} - \\\"${res.latestCommit.message}\\\"`);\\n        console.log(`Author:          ${res.latestCommit.author} <${res.latestCommit.email}>`);\\n        console.log(`Date:            ${res.latestCommit.date}`);\\n      } else {\\n        console.log(`HEAD Commit:     No commits found (empty repository)`);\\n      }\\n      console.log(`Working Tree:    ${res.uncommittedCount === 0 ? '\\\\x1b[32mClean (0 uncommitted changes)\\\\x1b[0m' : `\\\\x1b[33m${res.uncommittedCount} uncommitted change(s)\\\\x1b[0m`}`);\\n      console.log(`VVA Environment: ${res.isInitialized ? '\\\\x1b[32mInitialized (.vva/)\\\\x1b[0m' : '\\\\x1b[33mNot initialized (run vva init)\\\\x1b[0m'}`);\\n      console.log(`Python Runtime:  ${res.pythonReady ? `\\\\x1b[32m${res.pythonBinary}\\\\x1b[0m` : '\\\\x1b[31mNot found\\\\x1b[0m'}`);\\n      console.log('=============================');\\n      process.exit(0);\\n    }\\n\\n    if (command === 'report') {\\n      const commitIndex = args.indexOf('--commit');\\n      const targetCommit = commitIndex !== -1 ? args[commitIndex + 1] : 'HEAD';\\n\\n      const formatIndex = args.indexOf('--format');\\n      const format = formatIndex !== -1 ? args[formatIndex + 1] : 'all';\\n\\n      const dryRun = args.includes('--dry-run');\\n\\n      console.log(`\\\\x1b[36m[Stage 1/4] Git Data Collector: Inspecting commit ${targetCommit}...\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n      const res = await reportCommand({ commit: targetCommit, format, dryRun });\\n\\n      if (res.dryRun) {\\n        console.log(`\\\\x1b[32m✓ Dry-run completed. Saved project data to ${res.projectDataPath}\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n        console.log(`  Analyzed commit: ${res.analyzedCommit.slice(0, 7)} (${res.changedFiles} files)`);\\n        process.exit(0);\\n      }\\n\\n      console.log(`\\\\x1b[32m✓ Pipeline Execution Succeeded!\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n      console.log(`Repository:      ${res.repository}`);\\n      console.log(`Commit:          ${res.analyzedCommit.slice(0, 7)} (\\\"${res.commitMessage}\\\")`);\\n      console.log(`Feature Analyzed: \\\"${res.aiTitle}\\\"`);\\n      console.log(`Project Data:    ${res.projectDataPath}`);\\n      console.log(`AI Response:     ${res.aiOutputPath}`);\\n      console.log(`\\\\n\\\\x1b[32mGenerated Artifacts:\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n      for (const f of res.generatedFiles) {\\n        console.log(`  → ${f.filename} (${(f.sizeBytes / 1024).toFixed(1)} KB) in ${f.path}`);\\n      }\\n      process.exit(0);\\n    }\\n\\n    if (command === 'watch') {\\n      console.log('\\\\x1b[36m[vva watch] Starting Git commit monitor daemon. Press Ctrl+C to exit.\\\\x1b[0m');\\n      await watchCommand();\\n      // Keep process open\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    console.error(`\\\\x1b[31mUnknown command: '${command}'. Type 'vva help' for usage.\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n    process.exit(1);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error(`\\\\x1b[31mError: ${error.message}\\\\x1b[0m`);\\n    process.exit(1);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nmain();\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/commands/init.js\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import fs from 'node:fs/promises';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { isGitRepo, getRepoRoot } from '../core/git.js';\\nimport { getPythonBinary } from '../core/python.js';\\n\\nexport async function initCommand(cwd = process.cwd()) {\\n  const isRepo = await isGitRepo(cwd);\\n  if (!isRepo) {\\n    throw new Error(`Cannot initialize VVA: directory '${cwd}' is not a Git repository. Run 'git init' first.`);\\n  }\\n\\n  const root = await getRepoRoot(cwd);\\n  const vvaDir = path.join(root, '.vva');\\n  const logsDir = path.join(vvaDir, 'logs');\\n  const outputDir = path.join(vvaDir, 'output');\\n  const configFile = path.join(vvaDir, 'config.json');\\n\\n  await fs.mkdir(vvaDir, { recursive: true });\\n  await fs.mkdir(logsDir, { recursive: true });\\n  await fs.mkdir(outputDir, { recursive: true });\\n\\n  const pythonBin = await getPythonBinary();\\n\\n  const defaultConfig = {\\n    vvaVersion: '1.0.0',\\n    initializedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n    defaultFormat: 'all',\\n    outputDir: '.vva/output',\\n    pythonBinary: pythonBin,\\n    aiProvider: 'nvidia',\\n    aiModel: 'meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct',\\n    maxDiffSizeBytes: 1048576,\\n    team: {\\n      orchestrator: 'Abhiram Binil (Person 1)',\\n      aiEngine: 'Vishnu G Pillai (Person 2)',\\n      documentEngine: 'Vinay Bisht (Person 3)'\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  await fs.writeFile(configFile, JSON.stringify(defaultConfig, null, 2), 'utf8');\\n\\n  // Also ensure .gitignore ignores .vva logs and heavy artifacts if preferred\\n  return {\\n    success: true,\\n    root,\\n    vvaDir,\\n    config: defaultConfig\\n  };\\n}\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/commands/report.js\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import fs from 'node:fs/promises';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { getRepoRoot } from '../core/git.js';\\nimport { collectGitData } from '../core/collector.js';\\nimport { invokePythonModule } from '../core/python.js';\\n\\nexport async function reportCommand(options = {}, cwd = process.cwd()) {\\n  const root = await getRepoRoot(cwd);\\n  const vvaDir = path.join(root, '.vva');\\n  const outputDir = path.join(vvaDir, 'output');\\n  const configFile = path.join(vvaDir, 'config.json');\\n\\n  // 1. Ensure .vva is initialized\\n  let config = {};\\n  try {\\n    const rawConfig = await fs.readFile(configFile, 'utf8');\\n    config = JSON.parse(rawConfig);\\n  } catch {\\n    // Auto-create directory structure if running in uninitialized repo\\n    await fs.mkdir(outputDir, { recursive: true });\\n    config = { defaultFormat: 'all', maxDiffSizeBytes: 1048576 };\\n  }\\n\\n  const targetCommit = options.commit || 'HEAD';\\n  const format = options.format || config.defaultFormat || 'all';\\n\\n  // 2. Stage 1/4: Git Data Collection\\n  const projectData = await collectGitData(targetCommit, root, {\\n    maxDiffSizeBytes: config.maxDiffSizeBytes\\n  });\\n\\n  const projectDataPath = path.join(outputDir, 'project-data.json');\\n  await fs.writeFile(projectDataPath, JSON.stringify(projectData, null, 2), 'utf8');\\n\\n  if (options.dryRun) {\\n    return {\\n      dryRun: true,\\n      projectDataPath,\\n      analyzedCommit: projectData.analyzedCommit,\\n      changedFiles: projectData.changedFiles.length\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // 3. Stage 2/4: Invoke Python AI Engine\\n  const aiOutputPath = path.join(outputDir, 'ai-response.json');\\n  await invokePythonModule(\\n    'ai/ai_engine.py',\\n    ['--input', projectDataPath, '--output', aiOutputPath],\\n    root\\n  );\\n\\n  // Validate that ai-response.json was created and is valid JSON\\n  let aiData;\\n  try {\\n    const rawAi = await fs.readFile(aiOutputPath, 'utf8');\\n    aiData = JSON.parse(rawAi);\\n    if (!aiData.title || !aiData.summary || !Array.isArray(aiData.technicalChanges)) {\\n      throw new Error('AI response JSON is missing required fields.');\\n    }\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    throw new Error(`AI Engine verification failed: ${err.message}`);\\n  }\\n\\n  // 4. Stage 3/4: Invoke Python Document Generation Engine\\n  const docResultRaw = await invokePythonModule(\\n    'document_engine/document_engine.py',\\n    [\\n      '--ai-input', aiOutputPath,\\n      '--project-input', projectDataPath,\\n      '--output-dir', outputDir,\\n      '--format', format\\n    ],\\n    root\\n  );\\n\\n  let docResults = [];\\n  try {\\n    docResults = JSON.parse(docResultRaw);\\n  } catch {\\n    // If output contained non-JSON debug logs, check disk files\\n  }\\n\\n  // 5. Verify generated files on disk\\n  const shortHash = projectData.analyzedCommit.slice(0, 7);\\n  const repoName = projectData.repository;\\n  const expectedFiles = [];\\n\\n  if (format === 'pdf' || format === 'all') {\\n    expectedFiles.push(path.join(outputDir, `${repoName}_${shortHash}_report.pdf`));\\n  }\\n  if (format === 'docx' || format === 'all') {\\n    expectedFiles.push(path.join(outputDir, `${repoName}_${shortHash}_synopsis.docx`));\\n  }\\n  if (format === 'pptx' || format === 'all') {\\n    expectedFiles.push(path.join(outputDir, `${repoName}_${shortHash}_presentation.pptx`));\\n  }\\n\\n  const verifiedFiles = [];\\n  for (const f of expectedFiles) {\\n    try {\\n      const stat = await fs.stat(f);\\n      verifiedFiles.push({\\n        path: f,\\n        filename: path.basename(f),\\n        sizeBytes: stat.size\\n      });\\n    } catch {\\n      // File was not generated\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    success: true,\\n    repository: projectData.repository,\\n    analyzedCommit: projectData.analyzedCommit,\\n    commitMessage: projectData.commitMessage,\\n    projectDataPath,\\n    aiOutputPath,\\n    aiTitle: aiData.title,\\n    generatedFiles: verifiedFiles\\n  };\\n}\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/commands/status.js\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import fs from 'node:fs/promises';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { isGitRepo, getRepoRoot, getCurrentBranch, execGit, getCommitDetails } from '../core/git.js';\\nimport { getPythonBinary } from '../core/python.js';\\n\\nexport async function statusCommand(cwd = process.cwd()) {\\n  const isRepo = await isGitRepo(cwd);\\n  if (!isRepo) {\\n    return {\\n      isGitRepo: false,\\n      message: `Directory '${cwd}' is not inside a Git repository.`\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const root = await getRepoRoot(cwd);\\n  const branch = await getCurrentBranch(root);\\n  const configFile = path.join(root, '.vva', 'config.json');\\n\\n  let isInitialized = false;\\n  let config = null;\\n  try {\\n    const raw = await fs.readFile(configFile, 'utf8');\\n    config = JSON.parse(raw);\\n    isInitialized = true;\\n  } catch {\\n    isInitialized = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  let latestCommit = null;\\n  try {\\n    const headHash = await execGit(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], root);\\n    latestCommit = await getCommitDetails(headHash, root);\\n  } catch {\\n    latestCommit = null; // Repo might have 0 commits\\n  }\\n\\n  let uncommittedCount = 0;\\n  try {\\n    const statusRaw = await execGit(['status', '--porcelain'], root);\\n    uncommittedCount = statusRaw ? statusRaw.split('\\\\n').filter(Boolean).length : 0;\\n  } catch {\\n    //\\n  }\\n\\n  let pythonReady = false;\\n  let pythonBin = null;\\n  try {\\n    pythonBin = await getPythonBinary();\\n    pythonReady = true;\\n  } catch {\\n    pythonReady = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    isGitRepo: true,\\n    repositoryName: path.basename(root),\\n    repositoryPath: root,\\n    branch,\\n    isInitialized,\\n    config,\\n    latestCommit,\\n    uncommittedCount,\\n    pythonReady,\\n    pythonBinary: pythonBin\\n  };\\n}\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/commands/watch.js\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import { getRepoRoot, execGit } from '../core/git.js';\\nimport { reportCommand } from './report.js';\\n\\n/**\\n * Watcher daemon that monitors Git HEAD ref updates.\\n */\\nexport async function watchCommand(options = {}, cwd = process.cwd(), onCommitDetected) {\\n  const root = await getRepoRoot(cwd);\\n  let lastKnownCommit = null;\\n\\n  try {\\n    lastKnownCommit = await execGit(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], root);\\n  } catch {\\n    //\\n  }\\n\\n  const pollIntervalMs = options.intervalMs || 4000;\\n  let isRunning = true;\\n\\n  const intervalId = setInterval(async () => {\\n    if (!isRunning) return;\\n    try {\\n      const currentCommit = await execGit(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], root);\\n      if (currentCommit && currentCommit !== lastKnownCommit) {\\n        lastKnownCommit = currentCommit;\\n        if (onCommitDetected) {\\n          onCommitDetected(currentCommit);\\n        } else {\\n          console.log(`[vva watch] New commit detected: ${currentCommit.slice(0, 7)}. Generating reports...`);\\n          await reportCommand({ commit: currentCommit, format: options.format || 'all' }, root);\\n        }\\n      }\\n    } catch {\\n      //\\n    }\\n  }, pollIntervalMs);\\n\\n  return {\\n    stop: () => {\\n      isRunning = false;\\n      clearInterval(intervalId);\\n    }\\n  };\\n}\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/components/AIEngineView.tsx\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import React, { useState } from 'react';\\nimport { Cpu, CheckCircle2, AlertTriangle, Sparkles, Code2, Eye, ShieldCheck, Copy, Check } from 'lucide-react';\\nimport { Repository, GitCommit, AIStructuredResponse, VVAConfig, ProjectDataJSON } from '../types/vva';\\nimport { buildProjectDataJSON, generateStructuredAIResponse } from '../utils/orchestrator';\\n\\ninterface AIEngineViewProps {\\n  currentRepo: Repository;\\n  selectedCommit: GitCommit;\\n  vvaConfig: VVAConfig;\\n  lastAIResponse: AIStructuredResponse | null;\\n  onUpdateAIResponse: (response: AIStructuredResponse) => void;\\n}\\n\\nexport const AIEngineView: React.FC<AIEngineViewProps> = ({\\n  currentRepo,\\n  selectedCommit,\\n  vvaConfig,\\n  lastAIResponse,\\n  onUpdateAIResponse,\\n}) => {\\n  const [provider, setProvider] = useState<'nvidia' | 'gemini'>(vvaConfig.aiProvider);\\n  const [isAnalyzing, setIsAnalyzing] = useState(false);\\n  const [copiedJson, setCopiedJson] = useState(false);\\n\\n  const projectData: ProjectDataJSON = buildProjectDataJSON(currentRepo, selectedCommit, vvaConfig);\\n  const activeResponse: AIStructuredResponse = lastAIResponse || generateStructuredAIResponse(projectData, provider);\\n\\n  const handleRunAnalysis = () => {\\n    setIsAnalyzing(true);\\n    setTimeout(() => {\\n      const resp = generateStructuredAIResponse(projectData, provider);\\n      onUpdateAIResponse(resp);\\n      setIsAnalyzing(false);\\n    }, 600);\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleCopy = () => {\\n    navigator.clipboard.writeText(JSON.stringify(activeResponse, null, 2));\\n    setCopiedJson(true);\\n    setTimeout(() => setCopiedJson(false), 2000);\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"flex-1 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-4 w-full flex flex-col gap-4\\\">\\n      {/* Top Engine Control Strip */}\\n      <div className=\\\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 p-4 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg\\\">\\n        <div>\\n          <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-medium text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1\\\">\\n            Person 2 Module · Python AI Engine\\n          </span>\\n          <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n            <h1 className=\\\"text-sm font-semibold text-slate-100 flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n              <Cpu className=\\\"w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400\\\" />\\n              <span>NVIDIA API / LLM Code Intelligence Engine</span>\\n            </h1>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-xs text-slate-400\\\">by Vishnu G Pillai</span>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-3\\\">\\n          <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-slate-950 p-1 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs\\\">\\n            <button\\n              onClick={() => setProvider('nvidia')}\\n              className={`px-3 py-1 font-medium rounded transition-colors ${\\n                provider === 'nvidia' \\n                  ? 'bg-emerald-600 text-white shadow-sm' \\n                  : 'text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-200'\\n              }`}\\n            >\\n              NVIDIA API (meta/llama-3.1-70b)\\n            </button>\\n            <button\\n              onClick={() => setProvider('gemini')}\\n              className={`px-3 py-1 font-medium rounded transition-colors ${\\n                provider === 'gemini' \\n                  ? 'bg-indigo-600 text-white shadow-sm' \\n                  : 'text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-200'\\n              }`}\\n            >\\n              Gemini API (gemini-2.5-flash)\\n            </button>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <button\\n            onClick={handleRunAnalysis}\\n            disabled={isAnalyzing}\\n            className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-500 text-white rounded transition-colors shadow-sm disabled:opacity-50\\\"\\n          >\\n            {isAnalyzing ? (\\n              <>\\n                <div className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 border-2 border-white border-t-transparent rounded-full animate-spin\\\" />\\n                <span>Interpreting Diff...</span>\\n              </>\\n            ) : (\\n              <>\\n                <Sparkles className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5\\\" />\\n                <span>Re-Analyze with AI</span>\\n              </>\\n            )}\\n          </button>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      {/* Main 2-Column Split: Left = Structured JSON Contract & Schema Validation, Right = Interpreted Output & Anti-Hallucination Guardrails */}\\n      <div className=\\\"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-4 flex-1\\\">\\n        {/* Left Column: Output Contract JSON */}\\n        <div className=\\\"lg:col-span-5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col\\\">\\n          <div className=\\\"flex items-center justify-between pb-3 border-b border-slate-800 mb-3\\\">\\n            <div>\\n              <h2 className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-slate-200 uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n                <Code2 className=\\\"w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400\\\" />\\n                <span>Structured Output Contract (JSON)</span>\\n              </h2>\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\\\">Strict schema from Section 5</span>\\n            </div>\\n\\n            <button\\n              onClick={handleCopy}\\n              className=\\\"flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700 transition-colors\\\"\\n            >\\n              {copiedJson ? (\\n                <>\\n                  <Check className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 text-emerald-400\\\" />\\n                  <span>Copied</span>\\n                </>\\n              ) : (\\n                <>\\n                  <Copy className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5\\\" />\\n                  <span>Copy</span>\\n                </>\\n              )}\\n            </button>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Validation Chips */}\\n          <div className=\\\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-3 text-[11px] text-slate-400 font-mono\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-1\\\">\\n              <CheckCircle2 className=\\\"w-3 h-3\\\" /> title\\n            </span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-slate-600\\\">·</span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-1\\\">\\n              <CheckCircle2 className=\\\"w-3 h-3\\\" /> summary\\n            </span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-slate-600\\\">·</span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-1\\\">\\n              <CheckCircle2 className=\\\"w-3 h-3\\\" /> changedComponents\\n            </span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-slate-600\\\">·</span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-1\\\">\\n              <CheckCircle2 className=\\\"w-3 h-3\\\" /> technicalChanges\\n            </span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-slate-600\\\">·</span>\\n            <span className=\\\"text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-1\\\">\\n              <CheckCircle2 className=\\\"w-3 h-3\\\" /> technologies\\n            </span>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <div className=\\\"flex-1 bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-y-auto max-h-[540px] font-mono text-xs\\\">\\n            <pre className=\\\"text-emerald-300 whitespace-pre-wrap leading-relaxed\\\">\\n              {JSON.stringify(activeResponse, null, 2)}\\n            </pre>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        {/* Right Column: Interpreted Technical Meaning & Anti-Hallucination Guardrails */}\\n        <div className=\\\"lg:col-span-7 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col space-y-4\\\">\\n          {/* Card: Interpreted Feature & Changes */}\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"flex items-center justify-between mb-2\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-medium text-indigo-400 uppercase tracking-wider\\\">\\n                Extracted Feature Intent\\n              </span>\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400 font-mono\\\">\\n                Model: {activeResponse.model} ({activeResponse.processingTimeMs}ms)\\n              </span>\\n            </div>\\n            <h3 className=\\\"text-base font-bold text-slate-100 mb-2\\\">\\n              {activeResponse.title}\\n            </h3>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3\\\">\\n              {activeResponse.summary}\\n            </p>\\n            <div className=\\\"p-2.5 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-800 text-xs text-slate-300\\\">\\n              <strong className=\\\"text-slate-200\\\">Core Purpose:</strong> {activeResponse.purposeAndRationale}\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Card: Technical Changes Breakdown */}\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4\\\">\\n            <h4 className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-slate-200 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2.5\\\">\\n              Verified Technical Changes ({activeResponse.technicalChanges.length})\\n            </h4>\\n            <div className=\\\"space-y-2\\\">\\n              {activeResponse.technicalChanges.map((tc, idx) => (\\n                <div key={idx} className=\\\"flex items-start gap-2.5 text-xs text-slate-300\\\">\\n                  <div className=\\\"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 mt-1.5 shrink-0\\\" />\\n                  <span>{tc}</span>\\n                </div>\\n              ))}\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Section 5 Anti-Hallucination Guardrail: Facts in Code vs Assumptions */}\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 border border-amber-900/40 rounded-lg p-4\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2 text-amber-300 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2\\\">\\n              <ShieldCheck className=\\\"w-4 h-4\\\" />\\n              <span>Anti-Hallucination &amp; Grounding Guardrails</span>\\n            </div>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400 mb-3\\\">\\n              Per Section 5 of the VVA specification: <em>\\\"The AI should distinguish facts visible in the code from assumptions about the developer's intent. For example, it should not claim that a feature is secure or fully tested merely because a commit mentions authentication.\\\"</em>\\n            </p>\\n\\n            <div className=\\\"space-y-2 text-xs\\\">\\n              {activeResponse.observationsAndLimitations.map((obs, idx) => (\\n                <div key={idx} className=\\\"flex items-start gap-2 p-2 bg-amber-950/20 border border-amber-900/30 rounded text-amber-200/90 text-[11px]\\\">\\n                  <AlertTriangle className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 text-amber-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5\\\" />\\n                  <span>{obs}</span>\\n                </div>\\n              ))}\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Technologies Detected */}\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-3\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-medium text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-2\\\">\\n              Identified Technology Stack\\n            </span>\\n            <div className=\\\"flex flex-wrap gap-2\\\">\\n              {activeResponse.technologies.map(tech => (\\n                <span key={tech} className=\\\"px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-mono bg-slate-900 text-indigo-300 rounded border border-slate-800\\\">\\n                  {tech}\\n                </span>\\n              ))}\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/components/ArchitectureView.tsx\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import React, { useState } from 'react';\\nimport { Layers, ArrowRight, GitBranch, Cpu, FileText, Folder, Terminal, CheckCircle2, AlertCircle, FileCode } from 'lucide-react';\\n\\ninterface StageInfo {\\n  id: string;\\n  number: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  owner: string;\\n  technology: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  input: string;\\n  output: string;\\n  codeSnippet: string;\\n  errorHandling: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport const ArchitectureView: React.FC = () => {\\n  const [selectedStage, setSelectedStage] = useState<string>('stage-2');\\n\\n  const stages: StageInfo[] = [\\n    {\\n      id: 'stage-1',\\n      number: '01',\\n      title: 'Developer Git Workflow',\\n      owner: 'Software Developer',\\n      technology: 'Git CLI / IDE',\\n      description: 'The developer works normally, modifying code and creating commits. VVA requires no deviation from standard Git practices.',\\n      input: 'Developer edits, git add ., git commit -m \\\"...\\\"',\\n      output: 'Git commit hash, updated branch reflog, commit trees',\\n      codeSnippet: `git add src/tickets/ticket.controller.js\\ngit commit -m \\\"Add ticket filtering and status query parameters\\\"`,\\n      errorHandling: 'Developer continues regular workflow; commits remain local or remote.'\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: 'stage-2',\\n      number: '02',\\n      title: 'VVA CLI & Orchestration Layer',\\n      owner: 'Person 1 · Abhiram Binil',\\n      technology: 'Node.js (ES Modules), Child Process',\\n      description: 'Coordinates the entire system: verifies repository validity, checks if .vva is initialized, manages CLI arguments, and coordinates data flow between stages.',\\n      input: 'vva report --commit <hash> --format all',\\n      output: 'Process execution stream, logging, workflow orchestration',\\n      codeSnippet: `// src/commands/report.js\\nimport { GitCollector } from '../core/collector.js';\\nimport { runPythonModule } from '../core/python.js';\\n\\nexport async function reportCommand(options) {\\n  const repo = await GitCollector.detectRepository();\\n  const projectData = await GitCollector.collectCommitData(options.commit);\\n  await saveJson('.vva/output/project-data.json', projectData);\\n  \\n  // Invoke Python AI Engine\\n  await runPythonModule('ai/ai_engine.py', ['--input', '.vva/output/project-data.json']);\\n  \\n  // Invoke Python Document Generator\\n  await runPythonModule('document-engine/document_generator.py', ['--format', options.format]);\\n}`,\\n      errorHandling: 'Detects missing .git folders, uncommitted detached HEAD states, missing Python binaries, and reports clear human-readable remediation messages.'\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: 'stage-3',\\n      number: '03',\\n      title: 'Git Data Collector',\\n      owner: 'Person 1 · Abhiram Binil',\\n      technology: 'Git CLI (git log, show, diff, rev-parse)',\\n      description: 'Extracts commit-specific file versions, diffs, author metadata, and detects file status flags (A=Added, M=Modified, D=Deleted). Crucially retrieves the parent revision for deleted files.',\\n      input: 'Target commit hash, worktree path',\\n      output: '.vva/output/project-data.json',\\n      codeSnippet: `// Commit-Specific File Snapshot Extraction\\nexport async function getCommittedFileVersion(commitHash, filePath, status) {\\n  if (status === 'D') {\\n    // Deleted file: inspect parent commit (commitHash~1)\\n    return await execGit(\\\\`show \\\\${commitHash}~1:\\\\${filePath}\\\\`);\\n  }\\n  // Added or Modified: inspect target commit\\n  return await execGit(\\\\`show \\\\${commitHash}:\\\\${filePath}\\\\`);\\n}`,\\n      errorHandling: 'Handles initial root commits without parents (`--root` flag), skips binary blobs, truncates massive diffs exceeding 1MB limit.'\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: 'stage-4',\\n      number: '04',\\n      title: 'Python AI Engine',\\n      owner: 'Person 2 · Vishnu G Pillai',\\n      technology: 'Python 3.11, NVIDIA API (meta/llama-3.1-70b)',\\n      description: 'Reads project-data.json, constructs a rigorous system prompt, queries NVIDIA AI endpoint, and enforces strict JSON schema extraction with anti-hallucination boundaries.',\\n      input: '.vva/output/project-data.json',\\n      output: '.vva/output/ai-response.json',\\n      codeSnippet: `import json, requests, os\\n\\ndef analyze_changes(project_data):\\n    prompt = f\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Analyze the Git commit: {project_data['commitMessage']}\\n    Diff patch:\\n    {project_data['diff']}\\n    \\n    Return strict JSON with fields:\\n    title, summary, changedComponents, technicalChanges, technologies, observationsAndLimitations.\\n    Only cite facts supported by the diff patch. Do not guess untested capabilities.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    response = requests.post(\\n        \\\"https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions\\\",\\n        headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": f\\\"Bearer {os.getenv('NVIDIA_API_KEY')}\\\"},\\n        json={\\\"model\\\": \\\"meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct\\\", \\\"messages\\\": [{\\\"role\\\": \\\"user\\\", \\\"content\\\": prompt}]}\\n    )\\n    return json.loads(response.json()['choices'][0]['message']['content'])`,\\n      errorHandling: 'Validates returned JSON with pydantic; retries on schema deviation; catches API rate-limits with backoff.'\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: 'stage-5',\\n      number: '05',\\n      title: 'Python Document Engine',\\n      owner: 'Person 3 · Vinay Bisht',\\n      technology: 'Python, ReportLab, python-docx, python-pptx',\\n      description: 'Transforms structured AI response JSON into beautifully styled, standardized deliverables: PDF technical reports, editable Word documents (DOCX), and presentation slides (PPTX).',\\n      input: '.vva/output/ai-response.json, reusable templates',\\n      output: 'PDF reports, DOCX synopses, PPTX slide decks',\\n      codeSnippet: `# document_generator.py\\nfrom reportlab.lib.pagesizes import letter\\nfrom reportlab.pdfgen import canvas\\nfrom docx import Document\\nfrom pptx import Presentation\\n\\ndef generate_pdf(ai_data, output_path):\\n    # Builds multi-page structured ReportLab flowable\\n    ...\\ndef generate_docx(ai_data, output_path):\\n    # Generates academic synopsis document\\n    ...\\ndef generate_pptx(ai_data, output_path):\\n    # Creates 4-slide executive presentation\\n    ...`,\\n      errorHandling: 'Gracefully wraps overflowing bullet text, validates target folder permissions, enforces fallback fonts if system fonts are unavailable.'\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: 'stage-6',\\n      number: '06',\\n      title: 'Output Artifacts & CLI Feedback',\\n      owner: 'VVA Orchestrator',\\n      technology: 'File System (.vva/output/)',\\n      description: 'Saves all generated documents into the repository’s .vva/output directory and prints summary paths and success confirmation to the developer.',\\n      input: 'Compiled document files',\\n      output: 'Ready-to-submit files for academic evaluation, code review, or client presentations',\\n      codeSnippet: `[Stage 4/4] Document Engine: Completed ✓\\n✓ Generation Complete! Created output artifacts in .vva/output:\\n  → PDF Technical Report:    .vva/output/MiniDesk_e8f190c_report.pdf\\n  → DOCX Project Synopsis:   .vva/output/MiniDesk_e8f190c_synopsis.doc\\n  → PowerPoint Presentation: .vva/output/MiniDesk_e8f190c_slides.pptx`,\\n      errorHandling: 'Confirms file existence, outputs byte sizes, logs timestamps to .vva/logs/orchestrator.log.'\\n    }\\n  ];\\n\\n  const current = stages.find(s => s.id === selectedStage) || stages[1];\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"flex-1 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-4 w-full flex flex-col gap-6\\\">\\n      {/* Header */}\\n      <div className=\\\"p-5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4\\\">\\n        <div>\\n          <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-medium text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1\\\">\\n            Section 3 &amp; 7 · System Architecture\\n          </span>\\n          <h1 className=\\\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-100 flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n            <Layers className=\\\"w-5 h-5 text-indigo-400\\\" />\\n            <span>VVA End-to-End Orchestration Architecture Pipeline</span>\\n          </h1>\\n          <p className=\\\"text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1\\\">\\n            Interactive pipeline showing data transitions from Developer Git operations to AI analysis and final formatted document compilation.\\n          </p>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        <div className=\\\"text-xs font-mono text-indigo-300 bg-slate-950 px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-slate-800\\\">\\n          Git Records → AI Explains → Doc Engine Presents → VVA Coordinates\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      {/* Visual Pipeline Stepper */}\\n      <div className=\\\"grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-6 gap-2\\\">\\n        {stages.map((stg) => {\\n          const isSelected = stg.id === selectedStage;\\n          return (\\n            <button\\n              key={stg.id}\\n              onClick={() => setSelectedStage(stg.id)}\\n              className={`p-3 rounded-lg border text-left transition-all ${\\n                isSelected\\n                  ? 'bg-indigo-950/60 border-indigo-500 shadow-md ring-1 ring-indigo-500/50'\\n                  : 'bg-slate-900 border-slate-800 hover:border-slate-700'\\n              }`}\\n            >\\n              <span className={`text-[10px] font-mono font-bold block mb-1 ${\\n                isSelected ? 'text-indigo-400' : 'text-slate-500'\\n              }`}>\\n                STAGE {stg.number}\\n              </span>\\n              <h3 className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-slate-200 line-clamp-1 mb-1\\\">\\n                {stg.title}\\n              </h3>\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[10px] text-slate-400 truncate block\\\">\\n                {stg.owner.split('·')[0]}\\n              </span>\\n            </button>\\n          );\\n        })}\\n      </div>\\n\\n      {/* Selected Stage Detail Card */}\\n      <div className=\\\"bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-6 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6\\\">\\n        {/* Left Col: Explanations & Specs */}\\n        <div className=\\\"lg:col-span-5 space-y-4\\\">\\n          <div>\\n            <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-1\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-xs font-mono font-bold text-indigo-400\\\">STAGE {current.number}</span>\\n              <span className=\\\"text-slate-600\\\">·</span>\\n              <span className=\\\"text-xs text-slate-400 font-semibold\\\">{current.owner}</span>\\n            </div>\\n            <h2 className=\\\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-100\\\">\\n              {current.title}\\n            </h2>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-xs text-slate-300 mt-2 leading-relaxed\\\">\\n              {current.description}\\n            </p>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <div className=\\\"space-y-2 text-xs\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"p-3 bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1\\\">\\n                Technology Stack &amp; Libraries\\n              </span>\\n              <span className=\\\"font-mono text-indigo-300 text-[11px]\\\">{current.technology}</span>\\n            </div>\\n\\n            <div className=\\\"p-3 bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1\\\">\\n                Input Data Contract\\n              </span>\\n              <code className=\\\"text-slate-200 text-[11px]\\\">{current.input}</code>\\n            </div>\\n\\n            <div className=\\\"p-3 bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1\\\">\\n                Output Artifact / Payload\\n              </span>\\n              <code className=\\\"text-emerald-400 text-[11px]\\\">{current.output}</code>\\n            </div>\\n\\n            <div className=\\\"p-3 bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg\\\">\\n              <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-semibold text-amber-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1\\\">\\n                Robust Error Handling Strategy\\n              </span>\\n              <p className=\\\"text-slate-300 text-[11px] leading-relaxed\\\">{current.errorHandling}</p>\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        {/* Right Col: Code Snippet / Implementation Spec */}\\n        <div className=\\\"lg:col-span-7 flex flex-col bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs\\\">\\n          <div className=\\\"flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-slate-800 text-slate-400 text-[11px]\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-slate-300\\\">\\n              <FileCode className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 text-indigo-400\\\" />\\n              <span>Implementation Implementation Spec</span>\\n            </span>\\n            <span>VVA Coordination Protocol</span>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <pre className=\\\"flex-1 overflow-x-auto text-slate-300 whitespace-pre leading-relaxed p-2\\\">\\n            {current.codeSnippet}\\n          </pre>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"src/components/DocumentEngineView.tsx\",\n+      \"status\": \"A\",\n+      \"additions\": 0,\n+      \"deletions\": 0,\n+      \"content\": \"import React, { useState } from 'react';\\nimport { FileText, FileDown, Presentation, Eye, Download, ChevronLeft, ChevronRight, Maximize2, Minimize2, Check, ExternalLink } from 'lucide-react'